package docs

// ─── Overview ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
templ docsOverview() {
	@docsSection("overview", "Overview", iconCompass, "text-primary") {
		<p>
			<strong>Compass.AI</strong> is an AI-powered workspace and productivity platform that brings together
			conversational AI, a rich plugin ecosystem, and external service integration
			into a single, beautiful web application.
		</p>
		<p>
			At its core, Compass.AI is built around the concept of <strong>AI agents</strong> — specialized assistants
			that can be configured with unique personalities and tool sets. Whether you're
			a professional organizing projects, a researcher gathering data, or a developer exploring new technologies,
			Compass.AI adapts to your workflow.
		</p>
		@docsInfoBox("Key Concepts") {
			<ul class="space-y-2 mt-2">
				<li><strong>AI Models</strong> — Models from OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google Gemini with global per-capability configuration</li>
				<li><strong>BYOK (Bring Your Own Key)</strong> — Use your own API keys with decoupled per-capability provider configuration</li>
				<li><strong>Agents</strong> — AI personalities with custom prompts and per-agent tool configurations</li>
				<li><strong>Multi-Agent Workflows</strong> — Compose agents into sequential, parallel, and looping workflows, starting from a catalog of ready-made templates</li>
				<li><strong>Plugins</strong> — A rich set of built-in tool sets that extend what agents can do, useful for many agentic scenarios</li>
				<li><strong>MCP Connectors</strong> — Bridge to external services via the Model Context Protocol with OAuth 2.1</li>
				<li><strong>Personalized Profile</strong> — Your work preferences auto-injected into agent interactions</li>
				<li><strong>Threads</strong> — Persistent conversations with full history and file attachments</li>
				<li><strong>Memory</strong> — Cross-session recall with automatic preloading and on-demand search, enabled per-agent via the agent's memory settings</li>
				<li><strong>Artifacts</strong> — Versioned files created and managed by agents (reports, CSVs, images) with full version history</li>
			</ul>
		}
	}
}

// ─── Getting Started ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
templ docsGettingStarted() {
	@docsSection("getting-started", "Getting Started", iconRocket, "text-green-500") {
		<h3>1. Sign In</h3>
		<p>
			Compass.AI uses Google OAuth for authentication. Click <strong>"Get Started"</strong> on the home page and sign in with your Google account. Your account is created automatically on first login.
		</p>
		<h3>2. Create Your First Agent</h3>
		<p>
			Once signed in, you'll see the chat interface. New accounts start without any agents, so create your first one: open the <strong>Agent Designer</strong> (button in the top bar) and build an agent from scratch or start from a ready-made template. Then return to the chat and type a message to start a conversation.
		</p>
		<h3>3. Choose an Agent</h3>
		<p>
			Click the agent button in the message input bar (next to the attach button) to open the Agents dialog and switch between your agents. You can also open the <strong>Agent Designer</strong> and choose <strong>Browse Templates</strong> to explore workflow templates demonstrating multi-agent composition patterns.
		</p>
		<h3>4. Explore Features</h3>
		<p>
			Use the sidebar to access your conversation history (threads), filesystems, remote agents (A2A), tools (plugin management), and account settings. To attach files to a conversation, use the paperclip button in the message input bar. Each agent can be configured with its own tools, model settings, and instructions.
		</p>
		@docsInfoBox("Quick Tip") {
			<p>Press <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-border bg-muted text-xs font-mono">Ctrl+/</kbd> (<kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded border border-border bg-muted text-xs font-mono">Cmd+/</kbd> on Mac) anywhere in the app — or click the <strong>?</strong> button in the message bar — to view all keyboard shortcuts.</p>
		}
	}
}
